          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On September 12, 2021, at 01:15, two witnesses observed from their home the passage from north to southeast of a dozen \"orange points.\" The PAN \"all dim to about the same place.\" A photo is taken. Only one witness statement will be collected for this phenomenon. The witness description points to an observation of Thai lanterns, specifically:\n\n- **Appearance:** The description of points, orange color,\n- **Trajectory consistent with the direction and wind speed (see weather document) reported by stations in Bouguenais, 9km from the witness, and Saint-Philibert-de-Grand-Lieu, 18km from the witness (10° and 355°).\n- **Additionally, a lantern release can only occur with light winds, which is the case: 4km/h and 0km/h.**\n- **Disappearance of the phenomenon:** The dimming is typical of a lantern going out.\n- **Finally, the observation took place on a Saturday night to Sunday, a weeknight conducive to lantern releases, and the 5-minute duration is a typical length for a lantern observation.** However, no specific element (gendarmerie release statement) allowed to confirm the release, so the GEIPAN classifies this case as B: probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "a3761893855291c6f63c446b78655bb82fc52c93a2169c256f4cde26e03f662e"
        }
      ],
